_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mferlan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-05-26T13:28:43Z","updated_at":"2020-05-26T13:28:43Z","body":"> > * there is an empty file src/main/resources/META-INF/empty-beans.xml\r\n> >   (when this file is renamed to beans.xml then validation works)\r\n> \r\n> I'm very interested in knowing how you came up with `empty-beans.xml`. Was it something in the documentation that made you think this?\r\n\r\nThe intent regarding empty-beans.xml file remark is to point out that my attached project contained some \"commented out solutions\" and one of them was using empty beans.xml. So instead of deleting and recreating a file, for me it is far easier to rename a file and test if it works.\r\n\r\n**Regarding documentation**\r\nWhen I referenced model as dependency, then Quarkus build failed and one of the suggestion was to reference classes by quarkus.index-dependency in application.properties.\r\nThis resolved my build, but hibernate-validation  failed.\r\n\r\nSo after searching in guides for some clue, I ended up reading [Context and Dependency Injection Guide](https://quarkus.io/guides/cdi-reference). \r\nSo, next best solution seemed trying adding jandex-maven-plugin to my \"model\" project.\r\nThis failed, and then I started writing this bug and wanted to test on a clean project and tested empty bean.xml and it worked.\r\n\r\nI am fortunate that I can modify my \"model jar\" and add empty beans.xml.\r\n\r\nI am not sure if this is a bug or not.\r\nBut it seemed useful feature to have possibility to validate \"model\" from third party that does not have beans.xml (that is not bean archive).\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/634025163/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","a